and resume from Investments.

============================================================
39. COMPLETION LOGIC
============================================================

Completion must be calculated dynamically.

Example:

Income complete:

15%

Expenses complete:

20%

Savings complete:

15%

Investments complete:

15%

etc.

If a section is skipped:

It remains incomplete.

But the user can still use the application.

Do not block Dashboard access after initial setup.

============================================================
40. DATA COMPLETENESS VS USER ACCESS
============================================================

This distinction is important.

Profile completion affects:

QUALITY OF INSIGHTS

not:

ACCESS TO THE APPLICATION.

Never lock the application because profile completion is below 70%.

The user can always:

- Dashboard
- AI Copilot
- Budget
- Goals
- Profile

available according to existing navigation.

============================================================
41. AI COPILOT COMPATIBILITY
============================================================

The frontend should expose profile completeness to the Copilot context later.

Example:

profileCompletion = 65

missingSections:

[
  "loans",
  "goals"
]

Do not implement backend AI changes in this task.

Just make the frontend data model ready.

============================================================
42. EMPTY / MISSING DATA STATES
============================================================

When a section is not completed:

Use friendly empty states.

Example:

Investments

"Not added yet"

[Add investments]

Do not display:

₹0

unless the user explicitly entered zero.

Missing data ≠ zero.

